# The planning tool's own scratch state. It writes a checkpoint after every
# tool call, so a tracked copy is a file that changes on its own and turns up
# in unrelated diffs — and what it holds is one session's position, which is
# of no use to anybody reading this repository later.
/.planning

# Analysis caches, named in phpstan.neon and rector.php so CI can restore them.
/.phpstan-cache
/.rector-cache
/coverage

# The rule-proving harness writes a violation of every rule into the working
# tree, runs the analyser and the suite over them, and takes them out again.
# For the length of that run the files are really there — so git must not see
# them, or a commit made beside a run picks up a deliberate rule violation, and
# `git status` reports a dirty tree that is about to clean itself.
#
# Every path it writes sits under a directory called `Fixtures`, which is what
# makes one pattern enough. `tests/Support/Fixtures.php` is the registry itself
# and is a file rather than a directory, so it is untouched by this.
**/Fixtures/
.rule-fixtures/
# What a run has written, so the next one can sweep it even if this one is
# killed before its own `afterEach` is reached.
.rule-fixtures.written
.env.fixtureplanted

# Build output from the native expansion's two test harnesses.
#
# Also declared in `native/.gitignore`, and deliberately in both. That file only
# exists on a branch that has `native/`, so on any other branch the directory is
# untracked leftover from the last build — which is exactly when a wide `git add`
# sweeps 20MB of object files into a commit. This is the copy that is always
# present.
native/.build/
native/.swiftpm/
native/android/build/
native/android/.gradle/
